678
00:26:48,960 --> 00:26:53,960
to understand before we talk about

679
00:26:50,960 --> 00:26:53,960
optimization.

680
00:26:54,080 --> 00:26:58,960
To test our new function, we write a

681
00:26:56,000 --> 00:27:01,919
quick script. We choose a matrix size N,

682
00:26:58,960 --> 00:27:04,480
generate two random N byN matrices A and

683
00:27:01,919 --> 00:27:07,039
B, and call our matrix multiply function

684
00:27:04,480 --> 00:27:08,960
to compute the result. You can also

685
00:27:07,039 --> 00:27:11,440
compare it to Mat Lab's built-in

686
00:27:08,960 --> 00:27:13,039
multiplication to check for accuracy.

687
00:27:11,440 --> 00:27:14,960
And here's something to think about.

